Cookbook:Cassava|cassava]]\n* 1 [[Cookbook:Coconut|coconut]]\n* 4 [[Cookbook:Egg|eggs]] \n* 2 [[Cookbook:Tablespoon|tablespoons]] [[Cookbook:Cinnamon|cinnamon]]\n* 1 tablespoon [[Cookbook:Almond Extract|almond essence]]\n* 1 tablespoon [[Cookbook:Vanilla|vanilla essence]]\n* 200 [[Cookbook:Gram|grams]] [[Cookbook:Sugar|sugar]]\n* 75 grams [[Cookbook:Butter|butter]]\n* 1 [[Cookbook:Pinch|pinch]] [[Cookbook:Salt|salt]]\n* 1 big glass [[Cookbook:Milk|milk]]\n* 100 grams [[Cookbook:Raisin|raisins]]\n\n==Procedure==\n# Peel and grate the cassava. Grate the white coconut meat.\n# Beat the eggs and sugar until firm. Add the vanilla and almond essence. \n# Combine the eggs and sugar with the grated coconut and cassava. \n# Add the cinnamon, milk, raisins and salt. \n# Melt the butter and add it to the mixture. \n# Rub the dish you want to use with butter or use [[Cookbook:Cooking Spray|Pam]]. \n# Put the mixture in the dish. Put the dish in a pre-heated oven at 350°F (175°C). Bake the Bojo for about an hour. It needs to be firm on top but not dry on the inside. \n\n== Notes, tips, and variations ==\n\n* Sprinkle some cinnamon on top of the bojo before serving.\n\n[[Category:Surinamese recipes]]\n[[Category:Recipes for dessert]]\n[[Category:Vegetarian recipes]]\n[[Category:Recipes with metric units]]\n[[Category:Recipes using butter]]\n[[Category:Recipes using egg]]\n[[Category:Recipes using sugar]]\n[[Category:Recipes using cassava]]\n[[Category:Recipes using ground cinnamon]]\n[[Category:Recipes using coconut]]\n[[Category:Recipes using milk]]","isRecipe":true,"recipe":{"name":"Surinamese Cassava and Coconut Dessert (Bojo)","nameAr":null,"servings":null,"servingsSourceText":null,"ingredients":[{"id":"source-line-1","name":"1 kg cassava","sourceText":"1 kg cassava","amountText":"1 kg cassava","amount":null,"unit":null,"foodBinding":null},{"id":"source-line-2","name":"1 coconut","sourceText":"1 coconut","amountText":"1 coconut","amount":null,"unit":null,"foodBinding":null},{